      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301822",
      ":question/problem": "A warehouse stores $9,000$ light bulbs of assorted types. To estimate the percent that are LED, a random sample was taken. The percent of LED bulbs was estimated to be $24%$, with a margin of error of $3%$.\n\nIf $r$ is the actual number of LED bulbs in the warehouse, which of the following is most plausible?"
