      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301823",
      ":question/problem": "From a population of $50,000$ people, $1,000$ were chosen at random and surveyed about a proposed city ordinance. Based on the survey, it is estimated that $42%$ of people in the population support the ordinance, with an associated margin of error of $4%$.\n\nBased on these results, which of the following is a plausible value for the total number of people in the population who support the ordinance?"
